README Model Experience and bilingual-pair follow-up (2026-09-09)

Scope: complete the current package README acceptance closure for `ui-team` and remove stale tool-catalog links from private compatibility tool READMEs. This is a scoped documentation gate; it does not claim corpus-wide doc-sync, browser, multi-host, coverage, real-model, or release closure.

Changes:

1. `packages/client/ui-team/README.md` and `.zh.md` now use the audited short Model Experience form: one direct `None, as ... .` sentence, one `#### KV Cache effect` field, and one non-empty paragraph. The pair record was refreshed.
2. `packages/subagent/tool-subagent-control`, `tool-subagent-report`, `tool-subagent`, `workflow/tool-ralph`, and `workflow/tool-workflow` no longer link private compatibility tools to absent generated public-catalog anchors. Their model-experience headings now describe the local tool definition instead of claiming a generated catalog section. Five bilingual pair records were refreshed.

